course: dictionary
lesson: 12846
title: Endangerment: putting others at risk
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Endangerment means putting someone or something in danger. It is a noun, and it comes from the word danger. «Leaving the gate open was an endangerment of the sheep, because they could wander onto the busy road.»
explain: In law, endangerment is a serious crime. It means acting so carelessly that another person, especially a child, is put at serious risk. «The driver was charged with child endangerment after leaving the toddler alone in a hot car.» Nobody has to be badly hurt for careless acts to count.
explain: You will often meet endangerment in news and nature reports. Look at the words around it. Who is at risk? Was someone careless or reckless? If so, it is probably the law meaning. If an animal or a species is at risk, it probably means «endangerment of wildlife».
fact: Endangerment means putting someone or something in danger.
fact: «Endangerment» is a noun, and «endanger» is the verb: to put in danger.
fact: «Child endangerment» is a legal term for acting carelessly so that a child is put at serious risk.
fact: «Reckless endangerment» means putting others at risk by acting carelessly or taking big, foolish risks.
fact: In nature, «endangerment of wildlife» means human actions are putting animals at risk. This is why a species can become endangered.
exercise: «The careless driver caused the endangerment of the cyclists.» What does endangerment mean here? | Ending a race | Helping the cyclists cross the road | Painting the cyclists' bikes | *Putting the cyclists in danger
exercise: «The judge said the parents' reckless choices were a form of endangerment.» What is the best meaning of endangerment? | Helping someone out of trouble | Winning a prize for bravery | Telling a funny story | *A form of putting others at risk through careless choices
exercise: Which word is the root of endangerment? | Dinner | *Danger | Ranger | Manger
test: A nature report says «the endangerment of the tiger is caused by hunting and lost forests.» What does this mean? | Tigers are very happy and well fed | Tigers have found a new home in the city | Tigers are sleeping all day | *Tigers are in danger because of human actions
test: Which sentence shows child endangerment in law? | *A parent left a young child alone near a busy road, and no one was there to help | A boy helped his sister tie her shoes | The teacher gave the children a prize for reading | The baby slept soundly in her cot
exam: «The new law made reckless endangerment a serious crime, because careless acts can put others at risk, even when nobody is hurt.» What is the main idea? | *Careless acts that put others at risk can be a serious crime | Careless acts are always funny | Only adults can be in danger | Laws are boring to read
